# The whole bench session in the simulator: Developer > Bench session >
# Re-verify the video image, end to end, through the real menus.  The
# runner, the step table and order, the results file, resume, the
# auto-skips and the end summary are devbench.c's own; only the steps'
# device calls are the sim's stubs (apps/ipodui/devbench_sim.h says what is
# modelled and what is real: the job model's self-test, the probe image's
# block, the video player).  The restart (boot: the display driver)
# is a "reboot" part; the steps done
# outside the session are scripted (an album played, Now Playing opened,
# a video played, the wheel turned), then Bench session > Go on.  Every
# question gets its normal answer.  Sitting 4g's run: the held picks
# (BENCH_R_HELD: b3, s4b, s4c, vfeed, s7, vbv, vgov, respanel, c1,
# vizsoak, and with 19-9 retired clc, clf, ucop, uck1, uck2, ufeel,
# upanel, ucusb, ucmod, ucop2, ucoff) never show; the long play runs outside (vlong:
# the test episode on the video screen, its pictures in step with the
# audio, the minimum scaled to the clip).  vplay
# drops the unit's check result (a play before the session wrote one), so
# its play from Videos runs the first-use check (SIM_VCHECK: the model
# image counts as one with a clock token): its vck line, about 0.9 s, and
# the verdict on vplay's result line.  The end: bench_sim expect checks
# the results file: every pick once, with a result, in the picks' order
# (devbench.h bench_reverify_picks), the end line and the verified line;
# no clock150 token (s4c is held; 23693ff4's token is already granted);
# ucop is held, so the end clears the "cop" switch an earlier session
# left (bench_sim set ui_split cop at the start): the daily driver starts
# on the main processor.
# Sitting 4gh: the core layout probe's rows that may freeze (p2, p1)
# follow s6, and its dark row (duty) closes the run; the sim refuses all
# three (devbench_sim.c cop_row), so they skip and ask nothing.  The VC
# power rows (p19-vcpwr): s1, l5, ck before jvpu, vs after s6, sd last of
# all; the sim refuses them too (devbench_vcpwr.c vcp_sim_row).  The
# battery rows (p19-pwr-awake, p19-pwr-probes): pgrd, preg, awxm, prtc after
# pre, pldo then awld after ck, pstl, pden, psrf after awi2 (pden and psrf
# auto-skip on preg's sim skip); the cable steps
# (awd2, awd2c, awus) after s6, awi2 after p1, awlg's own dark soak before
# duty; the sim refuses them (devbench_awake.c, devbench_pwr.c stubs).
# Core layout A (p19-corelayout-k1): pcop after p1, k1 its own dark soak
# before duty; the sim has one core, so both say Not run (sim).
# Generated by scripts/bench_sim_script.py (normal); edit that, not this.
# needs: video
# golden: skip
# np: viz-full
# reset: viz
# log: vlong: PASS: pictures in step with the audio
# log: vf0: PASS
# log: ui switch cleared
# log: (ucop held)
# log: p2: Not run (sim)
# log: duty: Not run (sim)
# log: s1: Not run (sim)
# log: sd: Not run (sim)
# nolog: next start: ui cop
# env: SIM_VCHECK=1
# log: unit check: token dropped (bench reset)
# log: unit check: due (no token)
# logrange: 600 1500 vck PASS band 11 150 MHz tried 1 (\d+)ms
# log: video check: pass 150 MHz
# nolog: vck INCONCLUSIVE
# nolog: glass owned STALE
# nolog: bench_sim: watchdog
# timeout: 300
wait 4000
bench_sim reset          # no results files, the model's defaults
copy ../../bcmfw/video/vcheck.bin /.rockbox/vcheck.bin
rm_file /.rockbox/.sim_vcheck_band
rm_file /.rockbox/.sim_vcheck_bad
video_start /Misc/S01E03.m4v   # this unit's check result
wait 4000
video_stop
wait 500
bench_sim set ui_split cop  # an earlier session's switch
wheel +20 40            # the last row (Now Playing while music plays)
wait 400
wheel -1 200            # Settings
wait 400
key SELECT
wait 1200
key SELECT              # About
wait 1500
chord SELECT+LEFT 3200  # Developer
wait 1000
wheel +1 200            # Bench session
wait 400
key SELECT
wait 1200
wheel +40 10          # Re-verify the video image
wait 400
wheel -3 200
wait 400
key SELECT
wait 800
